    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1973641678314701062",
      "url": "https://x.com/ZiYuPh_Fanbase/status/1973641678314701062",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/ZiYuPh_Fanbase/status/1973641678314701062",
      "text": "@kooky__official\n\n1 minute before the voting ended and in the initial “finished” result shown, the vote counts for the other artist still changed — meaning a vote was entered and counted exactly at the closing time, not after the voting period had already ended. If the announcement takes 30 minutes to finalize because you say there was “traffic” in the system, then the first result should not have been posted as if it were already final.\n\nIf there is really a traffic delay, then why was a completed vote count shown in the first place? Fans were led to believe the results were final, and because of that, we could no longer act. Had we known that the numbers could still change after the closing time, we also would have dropped additional votes.\n\nThe point is: at the last minute and at the actual closing time, the ranking did not change. It only changed after 30 minutes — which you explained as “tallying due to traffic.” But this raises a very important question: why does it take that long if the final counts were already displayed? Showing a supposed “final” result and then changing it later is confusing and unfair to the voters.\n\nBecause of this situation, we strongly request for Ziyu to be removed from this voting platform. We do not want to encounter such unfair and misleading circumstances in the future.",
