    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1973649352016253210",
      "url": "https://x.com/ThaiEnquirer/status/1973649352016253210",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/ThaiEnquirer/status/1973649352016253210",
      "text": "If you are not attending the annual Navaratri festival at Sri Maha Mariamman Temple, also known as Wat Khaek, it’s best to avoid the Silom area this evening.\n\nYannawa Metropolitan Police Station has issued a traffic advisory announcing the closure of four main roads in Silom and Sathorn for the temple’s annual procession. The closures run from this afternoon until the early hours of tomorrow:\n\n- Silom Road (in front of Wat Khaek) from Nararom Intersection to Surasak Intersection: closed 16.00 – 04.00 hrs\n\n- Surasak Road: closed along the entire stretch 16.00 – 04.00 hrs\n\n- Narathiwat Ratchanakarin Road (inbound) from Narintorn Intersection to Nararom Intersection: closed 17.00 – 02.00 hrs\n\n- North Sathorn Road from Sathorn Intersection to Narintorn Intersection: closed 19.00 – 04.00 hrs\n\nAs no parking is available around the procession area, authorities recommend traveling by BTS Skytrain. The nearest stations to Wat Khaek are:\n\n- BTS Saint Louis Station (approx. 750 meters away)\n- BTS Surasak Station and BTS Chong Nonsi Station (approx. 800 meters away)\n\nThe BTS operates until midnight, though the last train departs from its originating station slightly earlier.\n\n#Thailand #Bangkok #วัดแขกสีลม",
